{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack","id":142651,"title":"[Flavor] How to do a Mixed Werewolf/Wolf-Blooded/Human pack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T13:55:26-07:00","id":142651,"title":"[Flavor] How to do a Mixed Werewolf/Wolf-Blooded/Human pack","content":"So first of all, sorry if this is posted earlier in the forum, I haven't checked OP forums for nearly 3 months.<br /> <br /> So my question is mostly just flavor and how to set up and describe a chronicle which features a pack with players playing more than just werewolves.<br /> <br /> So to frame my question is a description for what I planned to do for a Werewolf game set in Western Washington:<br /> <br /> -The players would play as werewolves from whatever tribe and none of them would know each other because they were each picked up by a different pack in different areas. <br /> <br /> - The Players would be put together in the middle of a forest, dropped off by the pack that found them and are expected to form a pack.<br /> <br /> - The story would be about surviving together and starting a pack and all the challenges that that would be about, while the following stories would be about the challenges of a pack carving out their place in the world and about the Hunt. <br /> <br /> <br /> With an update from Onyx Path about how packs can and often do have both wolf-blooded and human pack mates (just often without either of them being in the inner &quot;family&quot; circle of the pack, I was considering offering the players a choice if they wanted to play either a wolf-blooded or a Human at the character creation session. The one caveat would be that at least half would be Werewolves (with six players that would be 3 but I would prefer at least 4).<br /> <br /> <br /> So my question would be: would that work since wolf-Blooded are rarely allowed in the inner circle and as far as I could tell nearly never the human. The main theme that I am building for this chronicle the many challenges of the pack with pack life being the main feature for many of the following stories.<br /> <br /> My second question would be how to include Wolf-Blooded and Human Player Characters in a pack because I have a feeling W-B and Human PCs are a lot different than NPCs in how both the player's and I deal with them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:00:48-07:00","id":142692,"title":"","content":"I don't think it'll work. Troupes work better when their characters are peers, based on my experience. Furthermore, I'd rather wait for a more fleshed out description on how these dynamics work, and how the new Wolfblooded Merit works, Tells and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T19:48:22-07:00","id":142970,"title":"","content":"Why did a bunch of werewolves pick up some random humans and dump them in a forest with some werewolves? That seems like a weird thing to do.<br /> <br /> As I understand pack dynamics, you're always going to have the werewolves themselves as the core of the pack with the willing inclusion of other stuff because they were Important for whatever reason. Perhaps you have a totem spirit of diversity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T05:33:06-07:00","id":143323,"title":"","content":"Here is the wolf open development thread<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/open-development-projects/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/open-development-projects/\" target=\"_blank\"> Open Development &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/open-development-projects/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/open-development-projects/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:14:09-07:00","id":143784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=142970#post142970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did a bunch of werewolves pick up some random humans and dump them in a forest with some werewolves? That seems like a weird thing to do.<br /> <br /> As I understand pack dynamics, you're always going to have the werewolves themselves as the core of the pack with the willing inclusion of other stuff because they were Important for whatever reason. Perhaps you have a totem spirit of diversity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, More and more i'm thinking that I should go with what i was going to do at first and have all players be Werewolves and have the Wolf-blooded and Humans be important only after the pack is officially formed.<br /> <br /> My plan is actually to allow the players go out and look for a totem. The first story will be all about surviving the wilderness together and finding a spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:28:21-07:00","id":143786,"title":"","content":"If you have players who insist on being non-Werewolves in a Werewolf game, then what you might manage is that those players are discovered by the pack in the course of finding a totem and their help is so critical to actually getting the totem that they feel obligated to initiate them into the pack. You'd have to figure out the details on why they're there, why they're so instrumental, etc., which feels like a hard task since IC isn't out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:46:33-07:00","id":143801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=143786#post143786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have players who insist on being non-Werewolves in a Werewolf game, then what you might manage is that those players are discovered by the pack in the course of finding a totem and their help is so critical to actually getting the totem that they feel obligated to initiate them into the pack. You'd have to figure out the details on why they're there, why they're so instrumental, etc., which feels like a hard task since IC isn't out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't given them the idea that they can be anything other than a Werewolf yet and I wont make any drastic steps in making this Chronicle happen till Idigam comes out so I am mostly only in the pre planning phase.<br /> <br /> However your thoughts are really really helpful, thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T14:14:17-07:00","id":143860,"title":"","content":"That's about where I am in my Forsaken chronicle. Till then I run manitou springs, the 2 sas' that came out for forsaken and the one off storyline in the back of Hunting Grounds: Rockies.<br /> <br /> Might be the pack decides to investigate full moon murders (wolf blooded with the Uhran tell frenzy) and come across a wolf blooded. Rather then kill them (him or her) they take them in and use them as home defender of the territory. A dire wolf makes a far better defender then a haunted human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T21:32:17-07:00","id":144106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=143786#post143786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have players who insist on being non-Werewolves in a Werewolf game, then what you might manage is that those players are discovered by the pack in the course of finding a totem and their help is so critical to actually getting the totem that they feel obligated to initiate them into the pack. You'd have to figure out the details on why they're there, why they're so instrumental, etc., which feels like a hard task since IC isn't out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>As myself given a lot of thought on topic of <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> Wolf-Blooded...<br /> <br /> From what I read the article, Wolf-Blooded aren't invited to cul... packs inner circle out of politeness, only out of necessity. To manage new cult-like structure that pack and totem form, they <b>need</b> more than 3 &quot;person&quot; to run the pack. Also, if Uratha are hunting, someone need to look after they totem worship and lead the maidens to the alters. It's larger task, look in <b>Mage</b> - most cults need at least 3-4 Awakened to be run with, and we talk about guys having dynamic magic, not only minor gifts from great spirit.<br /> <br /> Also, werewolves are aware of they own mortality. They are violent race, and they know they quickly can perish on the hunt. But totem need to be attended, once the pack form bond with him. Wolf-Blooded makes great stewards of pack structure and &quot;spare Forsaken&quot; if someone will fall in battle. In other times, they can fill roles of regular Auspices that are short in the pack. And someday they could be proper Uratha.<br /> <br /> I encourage to give Wolf-Blooded Auspices persona ( not abilities ) with they Tells. If you need fan take on new Wolf-Blooded from spoilers, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded\">here is mine topic to make them a lesser template like new Ghouls</a>. And they work, as my players are happy with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=143801#post143801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't given them the idea that they can be anything other than a Werewolf yet and I wont make any drastic steps in making this Chronicle happen till Idigam comes out so I am mostly only in the pre planning phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be some time - now devs moved <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> till September, and as I saw the <b>Demon</b> development, it could be moved more. I would encourge to start game now, you could always help me playtest mine Wolf-Blooded take on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=143860#post143860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be the pack decides to investigate full moon murders (wolf blooded with the Uhran tell frenzy) and come across a wolf blooded. Rather then kill them (him or her) they take them in and use them as home defender of the territory. A dire wolf makes a far better defender then a haunted human.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Urhan Tell let you change in to regular wolf, not monster form. And from how I read, character can assume wolf form when he wants - only on Full Moon he <b>must</b> change, probably in Death Rage state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:01:50-07:00","id":144165,"title":"","content":"I just though about an interesting pack dynamic. Various wolf blooded members of a pack arpoach different and mostly unrelated werewolves. they tell them that their leaders perished in their last hunt and need werewolves to give porpuse to the pack. The werewolves must get to know each other and the wolfblooded try to keep the most control of their pack as they can. aditionally the werewolves might bring some trusted wolf bloodeds or humans with them. and the original pack might not like this newcomers usurping their places as most tursted members f the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:19:36-07:00","id":144587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=144106#post144106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Urhan Tell let you change in to regular wolf, not monster form. And from how I read, character can assume wolf form when he wants - only on Full Moon he <b>must</b> change, probably in Death Rage state.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he is in Death Rage, he is NOT in wolf form. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T11:33:33-07:00","id":144655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=144106#post144106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can be some time - now devs moved <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> till September, and as I saw the <b>Demon</b> development, it could be moved more. I would encourge to start game now, you could always help me playtest mine Wolf-Blooded take on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't start it right now. I am right about to start my Seattle: the Vigil Chronicle. I'm just planning ahead at the moment. However you make some valid points. Maybe some of my players want to start out Wolf-Blooded and play out the drama the typical werewolf troubles that many movies have and then later become full werewolf. It's a possibility I'm willing to entertain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T19:09:21-07:00","id":146254,"title":"","content":"Based on what has been teased so far, humans would be the ones &quot;maintaining the camp&quot; and doing the back up research, wolf blooded directing the camp's activities and being the intermediaries between human and Uratha (when the situation required) and possibly some light field support/reserve action. What I think could be interesting would be to have your players play both a werewolf character and a second human or wolf-blooded for when you want to shift Points of View and show what support work goes into any giver hunt. I've had success with that in past games.<br /> <br /> Here's something else you could consider. In my first Forsaken game the ST would let me play the NPC's in a scene where my character wasn't present or was in the background (He'd play my character based on the way I had been playing unless I said to do something differently). It worked really well (got me extra acting XP, that was nice) and made the game more fun. He gave a brief description and I'd improvise away, it's kind of disturbing at how much fun I had acting as the scumbag characters but it was fun seeing the other players have specific reasons to dislike the various &quot;bad guys&quot;. The other players liked it because it gave some diversity of voices to the antagonists, though none of them wanted to do it when offered the chance. I find if there's only one person playing all the bad guys they start to sound alike when they shouldn't (something I catch even myself doing as an ST, makes me feel like I'm shortchanging the players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). <br /> <br /> I have seen ST's that didn't do that, all had some theatre/acting background, but a really active and vivid imagination should be enough. Let the players try that if you don't want them playing multiple full characters, I think it may help them feel more vested in the story if they have a direct hand in personalizing NPC's, it definitely worked that way for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T12:14:35-07:00","id":146979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142651-flavor-how-to-do-a-mixed-werewolf-wolf-blooded-human-pack?p=146254#post146254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I think could be interesting would be to have your players play both a werewolf character and a second human or wolf-blooded for when you want to shift Points of View and show what support work goes into any giver hunt. I've had success with that in past games</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome. I might bring that up next week when we get together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}